#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:1
msgid "Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:3
msgid ""
"PyGMT's behavior can be controlled through various environment variables. "
"These variables can be set either in your shell environment or within your "
"Python script using the {py:data}`os.environ` dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:7
msgid ""
"Here we list the environment variables used by PyGMT which are categorized "
"into three groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:9
msgid "System environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:10
msgid "GMT/PyGMT environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:11
msgid "Module-specific environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:13
msgid "System Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:0
msgid "TZ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:17
msgid ""
"Specify the time zone for the current calendar time. It can be set to a "
"string that defines the timezone, such as `\"UTC\"`, `\"America/New_York\"`, "
"or `\"Europe/London\"`. Refer to [Specifying the Time Zone with TZ](https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/libc/manual/html_node/TZ-Variable.html) for the valid "
"format. If not set, the system's default timezone is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:23
msgid "GMT/PyGMT Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:0
msgid "GMT_LIBRARY_PATH"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:27
msgid ""
"Specify the directory where the GMT shared library is located. This is "
"useful when GMT is installed in a non-standard location or when you want to "
"use a specific version of GMT. If not set, PyGMT will attempt to find the "
"GMT library in standard system locations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:6
msgid "PYGMT_USE_EXTERNAL_DISPLAY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:33
msgid ""
"Whether to use external viewers for displaying images. If set to "
"`\"false\"`, PyGMT will not attempt to open images in external viewers. This "
"can be useful when running tests or building the documentation to avoid "
"popping up windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:38
msgid "Module-Specific Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:0
msgid "X2SYS_HOME"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/environment_variables.md:42
msgid ""
"Specify the directory where x2sys databases and related settings will be "
"stored. This environment variable is used by x2sys-related functions (e.g., "
"{func}`pygmt.x2sys_init`) to manage and access x2sys data. If not set, these "
"functions will use a default directory or prompt for a location."
msgstr ""
